// Escape Analysis (`EscapeInfo`, `FunctionEscapeSummary`) & Allocation Promotion (`opt_escape_promote`) Engine (T607 / E15.2).
// Implements SPEC-71 §§2-4 (AXS-ESC-001..004, AXS-ESC-010..017):
//   - Fine-grained `EscapeSet` bitflags + 4-tier `EscapeClass` lattice (`NoEscape < ArgumentEscape < ReturnEscape < GlobalEscape`, REQ-OPT-042)
//   - Distinct value escape vs. allocation escape tracking (`AESCAPE-26`)
//   - Interprocedural `FunctionEscapeSummary` & call-graph SCC fixed-point propagation (`REQ-OPT-043`, `REQ-OPT-045`, `REQ-OPT-357`)
//   - Mandatory 8-step `PhysicalStorage` decision hierarchy & observability barriers (`REQ-OPT-044`, `REQ-OPT-046`)
//   - `Box<T>` / `heap_alloc`+`heap_free` heap-to-stack & stack-to-SSA-register promotion (`REQ-OPT-335`, `REQ-OPT-346`)
//   - `NoEscape` closure capture environment scalarization & direct-call devirtualization (`REQ-OPT-336`)
//   - Bounded collection / inline `[C]T` buffer promotion & disjoint-lifetime slot reuse (`REQ-OPT-345`, `REQ-OPT-346`)
//   - `ReturnEscape` `NRVO` (`STORAGE_DECISION_CALLER_RET_SLOT`) & deterministic `--emit=escape` printer (`AXS-ESC-014`, `AXS-ESC-017`)
module compiler.opt.escape

